# Build context exclusions.
#
# node_modules matters most: the Dockerfile installs it in the `deps` stage and
# copies it in, and without this line the `COPY . .` right after would bury that
# under whatever is on the host — including native binaries built for the wrong
# platform, which is a confusing way to find out.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Build output. The image builds its own; copying a local one in also carries
# .next/dev/lock, which the prebuild guard would refuse to build over.
.next
.next-local
out

# Not part of a build
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
README.md
.screenshots
media

# .env is deliberately NOT excluded. NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined at build
# time, so NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL has to be readable during `next build` or the
# sitemap and share cards ship pointing at localhost.
